<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13658] Volatile cache writes to persistent storage.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13658</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Various cluster synchronization primitives (latch, lock, semaphore e.t.c) are using volatile cache (`default-volatile-ds-group`). State of this primitives does not make sense on storage (restore, recovery), primitive&apos;s state is useful only for process in action.&lt;br/&gt;
But it was stored in system data region.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;if (cacheType != CacheType.USER &amp;amp;&amp;amp; cfg.getDataRegionName() == null)            
 cfg.setDataRegionName(cacheProcessor.context().database().systemDateRegionName());
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which persisted if cluster have any persistent region:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;        addDataRegion(
            memCfg,
            createSystemDataRegion(
                memCfg.getSystemRegionInitialSize(),
                memCfg.getSystemRegionMaxSize(),
                CU.isPersistenceEnabled(memCfg)
            ),
            CU.isPersistenceEnabled(memCfg)
        );
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should to have dedicate system region for volatile cache, and it should be in-memory.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
